<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 2 August, from 216 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">216 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hannibal annihilates a Roman army at Cannae</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hannibal's Carthaginians encircled and destroyed a much larger Roman army in southern Italy, killing perhaps 50,000 men. Cannae remains the classic model of a battle of encirclement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1776</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delegates sign the engrossed Declaration of Independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Most members of the Continental Congress signed the parchment copy of the Declaration in Philadelphia. By signing, they put their names to an act of treason in British eyes.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1870</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tower Subway opens beneath the Thames</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A cable-hauled railway carriage began carrying passengers through the Tower Subway in London. Bored with a tunnelling shield, it was the world's first tube railway, though it closed within months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1923</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Warren Harding dies in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warren Harding died suddenly during a western tour, and Vice President Calvin Coolidge was sworn in by his father by lamplight in Vermont. The Teapot Dome scandal soon tarnished Harding's memory.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1934</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler becomes Führer on Hindenburg's death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Paul von Hindenburg died, and a law passed the day before merged the presidency with the chancellorship. Hitler became head of state and the army swore an oath of loyalty to him personally.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1990</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Kuwait</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Saddam Hussein's forces overran Kuwait in a matter of hours. A US-led coalition expelled them in early 1991, though Saddam remained in power.</p></li></ol>
